id: pm-yfdav2
title: Warn when custom schema fields collide with MCP transport or tool-specific inputs
description: "Surface a schema-author diagnostic when a runtime custom field such as cwd, path, options, or allowMissingParent cannot be projected as a top-level MCP input because a canonical transport/tool property owns that name. Preserve the collision-safe runtime behavior delivered in pm-xwah; report the conflict during schema add-field/profile/extension validation instead of emitting noisy MCP stdio runtime warnings."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 2
tags[4]: agent-ux,"area:mcp","area:schema",diagnostics
created_at: "2026-07-27T21:05:14.401Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-28T15:01:33.533Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: Schema and extension authors receive a deterministic collision diagnostic naming the custom field and canonical MCP property owner; Nested options remain available for the custom value and no transport routing semantics change
parent: pm-usfg
